# Prettier reformats the bodies of inline <script> blocks. index.html pins those
# by sha256 hash in its Content-Security-Policy, so formatting it invalidates
# both hashes and the browser then refuses to run them - silently. One of them is
# the theme bootstrap, so the visible symptom is the flash-of-wrong-theme it
# exists to prevent, with nothing in the console to explain it.
#
# scripts/check_csp_hashes.py catches this in CI; this file stops `npm run
# format` from causing it in the first place.
frontend/index.html

# The standalone bracket predictors: ~75-80 KB each, one large inline script,
# no CSP of their own. Reformatting them is a large diff with no benefit.
frontend/worldcup.html
frontend/ucl.html

# The Open Graph card sources. The portfolio card's terminal panel is a
# `white-space: pre` block whose leading spaces are the column alignment, and
# the two SVG motifs are hand-placed coordinate lists. Prettier reflows both.
scripts/social-previews/

# Generated locks and coverage artefacts.
package-lock.json
server/requirements*.txt
.coverage
node_modules/
dist/
# Generated by scripts/vendor_fonts.py, and third-party code copied verbatim.
frontend/fonts.css
frontend/fonts/
frontend/vendor/

# Vendored from Everything Claude Code (github.com/affaan-m/ECC) by its own
# installer, which compares content digests on upgrade. Reformatting them makes
# every future `ecc install` either refuse the file or silently replace it, and the
# diff would be noise either way. See docs/ECC.md.
.claude/skills/accessibility/
.claude/skills/context-budget/
.claude/skills/fastapi-patterns/
